{"availability":"available","full":"f-o-o-g-s/nokkvi","name":"nokkvi","description":"A rust based navidrome client for linux built using iced-rs","category":"Developer tools","language":"Rust","stars":44,"forks":4,"created":"2026-03-20T00:13:55Z","updated":"2026-10-09T19:16:55Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://f-o-o-g-s.github.io/nokkvi-docs/","topics":["desktop","gui","iced","linux","music","music-player","navidrome","navidrome-client","rust","subsonic","subsonic-client","wayland"],"demo":"https://f-o-o-g-s.github.io/nokkvi-docs/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.172Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.172Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.172Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.172Z","stars":44,"forks":4}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A native Rust/Iced client for Navidrome music server. Named after Old Norse nökkvi, a small, humble boat.","Demo of Nokkvi's GPU-accelerated audio visualizers and how the layout adapts to different window sizes.","⚠️ AI-Generated Project This entire codebase was written by AI (primarily Claude) with my direction. I'm not a developer. I come up with the ideas, test things, and use this as my daily music player, but I don't write code myself. You'll probably find patterns in here that experienced Rust developers would do differently. If you spot something that could be better, issues and PRs are welcome."],"features":["Native PipeWire audio engine: gapless playback, a 10-band EQ, ReplayGain and AGC normalization, and configurable crossfade with transition fades.","Opt-in bit-perfect playback (Strict or Relaxed, follows the native sample rate) with a badge that reads the real hardware clock as BIT-PERFECT, RESAMPLED, or UNVERIFIED.","GPU visualizer with bars, lines, and scope modes plus beat glow, bloom, trails, echo, reflection, horizon, a spiralling tunnel inside the scope ring, and CRT, shown in a band above the player bar or over the cover art,…","Theater Mode (F11): the playing track's cover, visualizer, and lyrics fill the window, with an auto-hiding player bar and optional fullscreen.","Smart playlists authored in-app: a rules editor with nested All/Any groups, live validation, presets, a raw-JSON mode, and server-evaluated previews. Also imports .nsp (needs Navidrome 0.61+)."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/f-o-o-g-s/nokkvi/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"20f0cf2a35a5f5e3542d4090db7010a828fed31e4b58fc618575583b5ac997c0","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.283Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.283Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A native Rust/Iced client for Navidrome music server. Named after Old Norse nökkvi, a small, humble boat.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/f-o-o-g-s/nokkvi/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"20f0cf2a35a5f5e3542d4090db7010a828fed31e4b58fc618575583b5ac997c0","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/f-o-o-g-s/nokkvi/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.284Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-09T19:16:55Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/f-o-o-g-s/nokkvi/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T19:34:19.285Z","hash":"20f0cf2a35a5f5e3542d4090db7010a828fed31e4b58fc618575583b5ac997c0","originalBytes":7860,"storedBytes":7860,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["nokkvi","navidrome","pipewire","player","build","cover","mode","rust","visualizer","arch","built","milkdrop","native","nokkvi-vx.y.z-x86","presets","queue","album","alsa-lib","bar","binary","config","docs","fontconfig","full","icon","install","install.sh","keyboard","linux","list","live","local","music","nokkvi-bin","optional","over","playing","plus","reference","release","window","above","art","audio","aur","band","bash","bit-perfect","butterchurn","clang","cmake","contributing.md","daily","desktop","download","each","engine","including","inspired","library","lyrics","m